/// How long a deferral is meant to last.
///
/// Deliberately two members and no third. TEMPORARY carries an end date;
/// INDEFINITE does not and stays in force until an authorized actor lifts it.
/// No clinical deferral *period* is implied by either -- the period is whatever
/// the staff member records, because no signed deferral schedule exists yet
/// (see docs/review-packs/clinical-review.md).
enum DeferralKind {
  TEMPORARY
  INDEFINITE
}

/// Where a deferral came from. Context, not a reason: the clinical reason lives
/// in `reasonCode`/`reasonText`, and `reasonCode` points at a vocabulary this
/// repository ships EMPTY on purpose.
enum DeferralSource {
  /// Raised at the chair, from a donation assessment recorded as DEFERRED.
  DONATION_ASSESSMENT
  /// Raised directly by authorized staff against the donor record.
  STAFF_DECISION
  /// Reconstructed by a migration from `DonorProfile.donorStatus = DEFERRED`,
  /// which carried no reason, no actor and no date. Provenance, kept honest.
  MIGRATED
}

enum ClinicalReleasePolicyStatus {
  DRAFT
  APPROVED
  RETIRED
}

/// The hard line between a policy a clinician signed and a stand-in that lets
/// developers exercise the code path.
///
/// This is not a flag on one policy kind: it partitions them. A
/// DEVELOPMENT_ONLY policy can never release a unit when NODE_ENV=production --
/// not by configuration, by refusal in `ClinicalReleaseService` -- and every
/// `ReleaseDecision` records which kind decided it, so no development
/// clearance can later be read as a clinical one.
enum ClinicalReleasePolicyKind {
  PRODUCTION
  DEVELOPMENT_ONLY
}

enum ReleaseDecisionOutcome {
  RELEASED
  REFUSED
}

/// Where a blood unit's ABO/Rh actually came from.
///
/// The system copies the donor's profile group onto the unit at collection.
/// That is a record of the donor, not of the bag, and this column is what stops
/// the two being confused (CL-05). UNIT_TYPED is reachable only once per-unit
/// grouping exists as a workflow; nothing in this repository sets it yet.
enum BloodGroupProvenance {
  /// Copied from the donor's VERIFIED profile group at collection. A record of
  /// the donor, not a result for this bag.
  DONOR_PROFILE_COPY
  /// Written down by the collecting staff at completion. Closer to the bag than
  /// a profile copy, and still not a laboratory typing of it.
  STAFF_RECORDED_AT_COLLECTION
  /// Typed from this unit by a laboratory. Nothing in this repository sets it:
  /// per-unit grouping does not exist as a workflow yet (CL-05).
  UNIT_TYPED
  /// Rows that predate this column. Their provenance is genuinely unknown and
  /// is recorded as unknown rather than backfilled with a guess.
  UNKNOWN
}

/// Where a blood unit's expiry date came from.
///
/// No component shelf life is encoded anywhere in this repository, so UNKNOWN
/// is the honest default and the one `ClinicalReleaseService` refuses to treat
/// as safe.
enum ExpiryProvenance {
  UNKNOWN
  /// Derived from a DEVELOPMENT_ONLY policy's `developmentShelfLifeDays`.
  /// Never a clinical shelf life; refused in production with the policy itself.
  DEVELOPMENT_POLICY
  /// Derived from an APPROVED PRODUCTION policy's shelf life. Unreachable until
  /// a clinician signs one.
  CLINICAL_POLICY
  /// Entered by staff against this unit.
  STAFF_RECORDED
}

/// What finally happened to a unit. The end of the traceability chain.
/// What finally happened to a unit.
///
/// Two axes, deliberately in one vocabulary because a unit has exactly one
/// final disposition. The first four are the blood centre's view of a unit
/// leaving its custody. The rest are the receiving hospital's view of what
/// became of it, which is the half that closes the traceability chain.
///
/// NO CLINICAL CLASSIFICATION IS ENCODED HERE. `REACTION_REPORTED` records
/// that a reaction was reported, not what kind: transfusion reaction
/// categories are a clinical vocabulary this project does not have (CR-08),
/// and the reported detail stays in the free-text context field.
enum DispositionType {
  ISSUED
  DISCARDED
  EXPIRED
  TRANSFERRED_OUT
  TRANSFUSED
  RETURNED
  DISCARDED_AT_HOSPITAL
  REACTION_REPORTED
  UNACCOUNTED_FOR
}

