/**
 * The lifecycle of a laboratory result, as the service already implements it:
 * values are entered, then verified by a reviewer, then published to the donor.
 * Was a free-text String. Nothing stopped a typo, and a misspelled status would
 * silently fail the `!== 'ENTERED'` guard that protects the review step -- so a
 * result could skip verification. The transitions live in laboratory.service.ts;
 * this makes the values themselves impossible to get wrong.
 * PENDING is the column's historical default and is retained so the migration
 * changes no behaviour. Nothing in the write path produces it: a result is
 * created as ENTERED.
 */
enum LaboratoryResultStatus {
  PENDING
  ENTERED
  REVIEWED
  PUBLISHED
}

