/// Why a unit is held. Holds are NOT lifecycle states: a held unit keeps the
/// status it had, and the hold is a separate record that refuses release.
///
/// Collapsing these into `QUARANTINED` was the available shortcut and would
/// have been wrong twice over. It loses the reason -- "reactive" and "dropped
/// on the floor" are not the same event to an investigator -- and, because
/// leaving QUARANTINED is `releaseUnit`, it would make lifting a hold and
/// clinically releasing a unit the same operation, which is exactly what the
/// product decision forbids.
enum BloodUnitHoldKind {
  REACTIVE
  ABO_DISCREPANCY
  TEMPERATURE_EXCURSION
  DAMAGED
  QUALITY_HOLD
}

